   "availability": "in_stock",
   "description": "The Mulholland Chronograph was designed as a tribute to the Santa Monica Mountains and the roads that shaped Southern California car and motorcycle culture. Its colors were drawn directly from the landscape—the muted greens of the hills, warm California sunlight, dry earth, and weathered asphalt. The sunray dial, shifting shades of green, and ghost bezel change throughout the day, while warm aged lume gives the watch the character of something that has spent decades beneath the California sun. On Mulholland, time has a way of forgetting which generation it belongs to. Early mornings at the Rock Store, afternoons at the Old Place, motorcycles disappearing into the canyons, and air-cooled sports cars winding toward the coast—it can feel as though little has changed since the 1960s and ’70s. An engraved map of Mulholland on the caseback completes the story—a tribute to the roads, landscape, and people who made these canyons legendary.",
